# What Docker may not send as build context.
#
# Without this the whole working tree is uploaded to the daemon on every build,
# which is slow at best and wrong at worst: a per-task worktree under .worktree/
# is a second full checkout with its own node_modules, and nothing in the build
# needs any of it. The context is what the Dockerfile COPYs from, so this is a
# correctness boundary as much as a speed one.

# Per-task worktrees: a second checkout, with its own node_modules and its own
# e2e/ that would shadow the real one.
.worktree/

# Version control and the git internals the worktrees live in.
.git/
.gitignore

# Installed dependencies. The image runs npm ci itself, so shipping the host's
# node_modules is pure weight and can carry the wrong platform's binaries.
**/node_modules/

# Run output. .e2e/ holds video recordings, which is exactly the kind of file
# that does not belong in a build context.
.e2e/
.e2e-report/

# Build and test output.
**/dist/
**/build/
coverage/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
**/*.egg-info/
*.test
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and editor noise.
.commandcode/
.harness-eval/
.omp/
.gstack/
.claude/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
